{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בסתר", :translit "ba'seter", :gloss "in secret"} {:he "בל' הרע", :translit "la'shon ha'ra", :gloss "evil tongue"} {:he "מסר ממון חבירו", :translit "masar mamon chaveiro", :gloss "delivered his fellow's money"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "בסתר", :b "בל' הרע"} {:kind :gematria, :a "בסתר", :b "מסר ממון חבירו"}], :frame {:text "The phrase בסתר ('in secret') in the context of the curse against one who strikes his fellow secretly is read as encoding two transgressions. The verse adjacent to this one, Deuteronomy 27:25, curses one who takes a bribe to strike (נגח), which the Sages interpret as delivering false testimony or money fraudulently, as in the phrase מכה רשע (Exodus 22:8 understood per Sanhedrin 7b as financial betrayal). Leviticus 19:16 prohibits going about as a talebearer (רכיל), which the Sages equate to lashon ha-ra (Erchin 15b).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 27:25" "Leviticus 19:16" "Sanhedrin 7b" "Erchin 15b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "בסתר", :a-value 662, :b "בל' הרע", :b-value 307, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "בסתר", :a-value 662, :b "מסר ממון חבירו", :b-value 662, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:50.395913049Z", :model "glm-5.2"}